IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tfm-dates`
IMPORT `tfm-rules`
IMPORT `tfm-seat`
IMPORT `tfm-seat-beneficiary`

-- Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) -- worked cases for the beneficiary's questions
-- (tfm-seat-beneficiary.l4), with mirror cases asking the same facts from the claimant's seat (tfm-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion
-- is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 4(2) -- service of the summons`

#ASSERT `Must the claimant's summons be served on me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the claimant's summons be served on me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the claimant's summons be served on me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 10A -- my part of the provision`

-- $100 000 ordered; my part $300 000 of a $600 000 estate: half, $50 000.
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 100000 300000 600000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 50000
-- $90 000 ordered; my part $100 000 of $300 000: a third, $30 000.
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 90000 100000 300000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 30000
-- The sole beneficiary bears it all.
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 40000 200000 200000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 40000
-- Exonerated (s 10A(2)); outside the Court's authority (s 10A(1)).
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 100000 300000 600000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 100000 300000 600000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- "unless the Court ... otherwise orders": its order decides (fork F8).
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 100000 300000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` 100000 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 9(5A), 11(4) -- what was distributed to me`

#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `a claim needing an extension of time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `a claim needing an extension of time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `an application to alter an order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9(5A) protects only a distribution "lawfully made".
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `an application to alter an order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `an application to alter an order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A claim in time: the Act is silent (fork F9).
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `a claim taken out within the time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 9(5) -- applying to rescind or alter the order`

#ASSERT `Can I apply to rescind or alter the order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to rescind or alter the order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to rescind or alter the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `mirror cases -- the same facts from both seats`

-- A claimant out of time; the estate partly distributed to the beneficiary, not finally. The claimant may still apply
-- for more time (s 11(2)-(4)); what the beneficiary already received before that application cannot be disturbed
-- (s 11(4)). The two answers agree: the extension reaches only what is left.
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for more time` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` `a claim needing an extension of time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The beneficiary applies to alter the claimant's order; the claimant takes a benefit under it. The beneficiary may
-- apply (s 9(5)); the claimant must be served with notice (s 9(6)).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to rescind or alter the order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be served with notice of an application to change the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
